{"tool_name":"refernment","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ReFernment","home":"https://github.com/TARobison/ReFernment","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"R package for annotating RNA editing in plastid genomes.","addition_date":"2019-05-18T08:44:32Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:22Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["1.1.2"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:ReFernment","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"robison.tanner@gmail.com","name":"Tanner Robison","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"},{"term":"Editing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3096"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"ReFernment","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1002/aps3.1216","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 Robison and Wolf Applications in Plant Sciences is published by Wiley Periodicals, Inc. on behalf of the Botanical Society of AmericaPremise of the Study: In the absence of cDNA, the annotation of RNA editing in plastomes must be done manually, representing a significant time cost to those studying the organellar genomes of ferns and hornworts. Methods and Results: We developed an R package to automatically annotate apparent nonsense mutations in plastid genomes. The software successfully annotates such sites and results in no false positives for data with no sequencing or assembly errors. Conclusions: Compared to manual annotation, ReFernment offers greater speed and accuracy for annotating RNA editing sites. This software should be especially useful for researchers generating large numbers of plastome sequences for taxa with high levels of RNA editing.","authors":[{"name":"Robison T.A."},{"name":"Wolf P.G."}],"citationCount":3,"d